    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d856">

                <pb facs="0925" n="1759" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1759"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.711/2551</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9552</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received August 1.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 9275, of June
                    7, and my telegram No. 18 of July 1 replying to the Department’s telegram No.
                    8508 of June 29, 3 p.m., relative to the censorship of diplomatic correspondence
                    passing in transit through Great Britain, I have the honor to enclose herewith
                    copy of a note from the Foreign Office, dated July 11, 1918,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d856-f1"/> in which it is stated, in order to remove any uncertainty
                    which may prevail as to the scope of the Foreign Office circular note of May 31
                        last,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d856-f2"/> that it is not intended to apply the
                    measures set forth therein to the correspondence of the United States
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Irwin Laughlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
